=====================
USEFUL AV.ONE COMMANDS
=====================

CAN SETUP
  - Bring up physical SocketCAN interface (can0)
  - Create a virtual CAN interface for testing (vcan0)

  CAN0 (physical bus, 250k):
    sudo ip link set can0 down
    sudo ip link set can0 type can bitrate 250000
    sudo ip link set can0 up

  VCAN0 (virtual bus):
    sudo modprobe vcan
    sudo ip link add dev vcan0 type vcan
    sudo ip link set up vcan0


GPS
  - NMEA serial driver for GPS over USB serial

  Command:
    ros2 run nmea_navsat_driver nmea_serial_driver \
      --ros-args \
      -p port:=/dev/ttyUSB1 \
      -p baud:=115200 \
      -p frame_id:=base_link


LIDAR
  - Launch Quanergy client and publish a static TF for the sensor frame

  Quanergy driver:
    ros2 launch quanergy_client_ros client.launch.py host:=192.168.1.57

  Static TF (laser_frame -> quanergy):
    ros2 run tf2_ros static_transform_publisher \
      0 0 0 0 0 0 laser_frame quanergy


STATIC TF
  - Map to Odom (useful when you want a fixed frame without full localisation)

  Command:
    ros2 run tf2_ros static_transform_publisher \
      0 0 0 0 0 0 map odom


INTEL REALSENSE D435
  - Single D435 launch (RGB + Depth + Pointcloud + aligned depth)

  Command:
    ros2 launch realsense2_camera rs_launch.py \
      enable_color:=true \
      enable_depth:=true \
      rgb_camera.profile:=1920x1080x30 \
      depth_module.profile:=1920x1080x30 \
      pointcloud.enable:=true \
      align_depth.enable:=true


KEYBOARD TELEOP
  - Send Twist commands to the Ackermann controller reference topic

  Command:
    ros2 run teleop_twist_keyboard teleop_twist_keyboard \
      --ros-args \
      --remap cmd_vel:=/ackermann_steering_controller/reference \
      -p repeat_rate:=10.0 \
      -p stamped:=true
